;; clojure-lsp configuration for Jonquil.
;;
;; :cljfmt matches the formatter to the style already in the tree, rather
;; than reformatting the tree to the formatter's default. clojure-lsp's
;; default splits a map literal one key-value pair per line; Jonquil writes
;; short maps compactly, e.g.
;;
;;   {:edits [[0 (count text) out]] :caret (min caret (count out)) :sel nil}
;;
;; Measured 2026-09-26 (clojure-lsp 2026.05.05-12.58.26): with the default,
;; `format --dry` over src/test/dev (minus dev/smoke/fixtures, see below)
;; wanted 34 files reformatted, nearly all of them this one rule. With this
;; setting, 13 remain — the rest are genuine indentation differences, not
;; this rule. One setting instead of a 34-file churn commit.
;;
;; No :project-specs override: unlike a-private-sibling's AppKit/UIKit siblings,
;; deps.edn here has no :deps map (jolt.ffi is a runtime builtin, not a
;; resolved dependency) and no :local/root sibling checkout, so the default
;; classpath heuristic resolves cleanly on its own.
;;
;; Not set here, because neither `bb lsp:*` task nor this file can fix it:
;; dev/smoke/fixtures/*.clj are deliberately invalid or minimal Clojure
;; (binary_smoke.clj feeds them to the built jonquil binary to exercise
;; unclosed-paren recovery, completion, find, etc.). clojure-lsp's `format`
;; and `clean-ns` commands parse every file under a discovered source-path
;; with rewrite-clj, which throws a hard "Unexpected EOF" on
;; fixtures/unclosed.clj and aborts the WHOLE run — measured against this
;; same clojure-lsp build, both with no scoping and with
;; :source-paths-ignore-regex targeting the fixtures path (neither stops the
;; crash, because "dev" is itself the discovered source-path and the
;; ignore-regex only filters candidate source-path roots, not files
;; underneath one already chosen). The `.clj-kondo/config.edn`
;; :output {:exclude-files} entry doesn't help either — that only silences
;; clj-kondo's own diagnostics, and format/clean-ns don't consult it. The
;; working fix lives in bb.edn's `lsp-filenames`, which passes format and
;; clean-ns an explicit comma-separated --filenames list (src, test, and
;; every real dev entry) that never includes dev/smoke/fixtures.
{:cljfmt {:split-keypairs-over-multiple-lines? false
          ;; gtk-async/go-row (dev/gtk_async.clj): a row's steps indent as a
          ;; block body, two spaces in, instead of aligning under the macro's
          ;; first argument (measured: the default wants the body 10 columns in).
          :extra-indents {go-row [[:block 2]]}}}
